{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 18:41:24.242698", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### **Network Health Overview**\\nThe network appears to have significant connectivity issues, particularly between hosts and other devices. While some devices are able to communicate successfully, others are unable to establish connections, indicating potential anomalies in the network.\\n\\n#### **Findings**\\n1. **Host Connectivity Issues**:\\n   - **Host `host_1_1_1_1`**:\\n     - Unable to reach `host_2_1_1_1`.\\n     - Unable to reach `web_server_1`.\\n   - **Host `host_2_1_1_1`**:\\n     - Unable to reach `web_server_1`.\\n     - No connectivity with other devices.\\n\\n2. **Server Communication**:\\n   - **DHCP Server**:\\n     - Successfully communicates with `web_server_1` (0% packet loss, average RTT: 1.095 ms).\\n     - Unable to reach `host_2_1_1_1`.\\n   - **DNS Server**:\\n     - Successfully communicates with `web_server_1` (0% packet loss, average RTT: 1.147 ms).\\n     - Unable to reach `host_2_1_1_1`.\\n   - **Load Balancer**:\\n     - Successfully communicates with `web_server_1` (0% packet loss, average RTT: 1.086 ms).\\n     - Unable to reach `host_2_1_1_1`.\\n\\n3. **Web Server Communication**:\\n   - All web servers (`web_server_0`, `web_server_1`, `web_server_2`, `web_server_3`) successfully communicate with each other (0% packet loss, average RTTs ranging from 1.036 ms to 1.392 ms).\\n   - None of the web servers can reach `host_2_1_1_1`.\\n\\n4. **General Observations**:\\n   - Communication between infrastructure devices (e.g., servers and load balancer) is functional.\\n   - Hosts are isolated and unable to communicate with other devices, including servers and each other.\\n\\n#### **Potential Anomalies**\\n- **Host Isolation**:\\n  - Both `host_1_1_1_1` and `host_2_1_1_1` are unable to communicate with other devices, suggesting issues at the access layer (e.g., access switches or distribution routers).\\n- **Access Switches or Router Issues**:\\n  - The inability of hosts to reach servers or other hosts may indicate misconfigurations or failures in the access switches (`switch_access_1_1_1`, `switch_access_2_1_1`) or distribution routers (`router_dist_1_1`, `router_dist_2_1`).\\n\\n#### **Next Steps**\\nFurther investigation is required to pinpoint the root cause of the host isolation. This may involve:\\n- Verifying the configuration and operational status of access switches and distribution routers.\\n- Checking OSPF configurations and routing tables on the routers.\\n- Examining DHCP relay functionality to ensure hosts are receiving proper IP configurations.\\n\\nThis concludes the diagnostic report., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='e3ed3a28-9df0-44bc-98be-e431e6928502'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
